1. A container for separately storing and selectively mixing first and second fluids, the container comprising:

a body defining an interior volume;

a rupturable membrane disposed within the interior volume and dividing the interior volume into a first compartment configured to contain the first fluid and a second compartment configured to contain the second fluid, the rupturable membrane being configured to maintain the first and second fluids separated during storage;

a flexible wall portion forming at least part of the body and being deformable inwardly in response to manual pressure applied externally to the container; and

a striker coupled to or carried by the flexible wall portion and positioned to move toward the rupturable membrane upon inward deformation of the flexible wall portion,

wherein deformation of the flexible wall portion drives the striker into engagement with the rupturable membrane to rupture the rupturable membrane, thereby placing the first compartment and the second compartment in fluid communication and permitting the first and second fluids to mix within the interior volume.

1. A container for selectively mixing two fluids, comprising:

a first body defining a first chamber configured to contain a first fluid;

a second body defining a second chamber configured to contain a second fluid, the second body being received at least partially within the first chamber of the first body;

a frangible or rupturable barrier separating the second chamber from the first chamber; and

a striker fixed to a pliable closed end of the container,

wherein the pliable closed end is deformable by user-applied pressure to displace the striker toward the second body or the barrier, thereby rupturing the barrier and placing the second chamber in fluid communication with the first chamber to mix the first fluid and the second fluid on demand.
